 "brief": {
  "may_change": [],
  "may_relax": [],
  "objective": "time",
  "quantity": 10,
  "text": "An angle bracket that holds the end of a lead screw to a frame. Its mounting leg is bolted to the frame by two M5 bolts and must sit flat on it; its other leg carries the screw in a hole at its end, and the screw's thrust pushes that leg outwards. The bracket is made as drawn: its shape and sizes are fixed by the frame and the screw. Printed in PLA on the lab's CORE One+ in a small series; print time matters most."
 },
